**`convolve_{x,y,2d}_sr` get `_v4` arms — the largest mapped C-AVX-512 gap
remaining after SAD + variance.** Third target of the AVX-512 coverage
campaign. The inter delta (`~/tmp/cg-inter/delta_port_*`, callgrind — prices
the `_v3` arm on this host; valgrind 3.27.1 cannot run zmm) put the three
kernels at 15.9M + 13.9M + 8.4M self Ir = ~8.9% of the port-vs-C inter-frame
delta on gradient p8. C registers all three at AVX-512
(`convolve_avx512.c`, `convolve_2d_avx512.c`).

date:   2026-09-19
host:   r7900x — AMD Ryzen 9 7900X, **Zen 4: AVX-512 double-pumped over
        256-bit units**. A 512-bit arm buys instruction count and front-end
        width, NOT execution width. perf_event_paranoid=4: NO hardware
        counters — wall clock is the only real measurement.
base:   `1d4421242` — variance `_v4` + subpel dead-end commit (so this A/B
        isolates convolve).
cand:   working tree — `crates/svtav1-dsp/src/port_convolve.rs`.
data:   benchmarks/convolve_sr_avx512_inter_grad.ab.{tsv,raw.tsv}  (48r w16)
        benchmarks/convolve_sr_avx512_still_grad.ab.{tsv,raw.tsv}  (16r still)

========================= 1. WHAT LANDS =========================

`port_convolve.rs`: three `#[arcane]` v4 kernels dispatched at `w >= 16`
before the `_v3` arm (narrower blocks keep `_v3`):

- `convolve_x_sr_v4` / `convolve_y_sr_v4` / `convolve_2d_sr_v4` — the v3
  lanewise pipelines at 32 output pixels/iter (ymm loads ->
  `_mm512_cvtepu8_epi16` -> `i16 mullo` -> halves widened to `i32x16`
  accumulators), plus a 16-px rung (xmm load -> ymm widen -> single
  `i32x16` acc) and a scalar tail.

Semantics preserved exactly:

- ordered narrows via `vpmovsdw`/`vpmovuswb` — `packs`'s 128-bit lane
  interleave is never used, so no permute fixups;
- `round_power_of_two(v, 0) = v`: `bits` is **0** for single prediction
  (round_0=3, round_1=11), so `b_off`/`bv` are `bits.max(0)`-guarded —
  `1 << -1` would panic;
- `as i16` truncation in `convolve_2d_sr` is `vpmovdw` (truncate), not
  `vpmovsdw` (saturate); the vertical pass truncates then re-widens to i32
  for the final `round_power_of_two(.., bits)` exactly like the scalar arm;
- separate source-boundary bounds per rung (`x1_32` / `x1_16`); edge columns
  go scalar as in v3.

Gate at `w >= 16`, not `w >= 8`: the 8-px path would be xmm-identical to
v3 with EVEX context on top — the subpel dead end showed that buys nothing
on Zen 4.

========================= 2. RESULTS (Zen 4, wall clock) =========================

Interleaved paired A/B, `tools/perf_ab.sh`, gradient 512², inter cell
(SVTAV1_FRAMES=4 FRAME_SHIFT=3 INTRA_PERIOD=64 HIER_LEVELS=0
INTER_EXPERIMENTAL=1). `ident=Y` on every measured cell.

  w>=32 only, 24r:    p6 0.9953 [0.9933, 1.0001]  p8 0.9972 [0.9950, 1.0005]
                      (median win but p25/p75 straddle — not disjoint)
  w>=16,     48r:     p6 0.9917 [0.9876, 0.9969]  p8 0.9920 [0.9891, 0.9960]
                      **disjoint win, ~0.8% both presets** — the 16-px rung
                      roughly doubled the effect.
  still 512 p6, 16r:  1.0054 [0.9982, 1.0167] — flat (convolve_sr is
                      inter-only; spans 1.0 = noise).

Numbers are Zen-4-specific; full-width 512-bit silicon is unmeasured.

========================= 3. GATES =========================

- `cargo nextest run -p zenav1-svt-dsp --locked`: 847/847 (incl.
  c_parity_port_convolve 10/10 — real C FFI oracle across filters × sizes
  up to 64×64 × phases; exercises the v4 rungs on this host).
- `cargo nextest run --workspace --locked --test-threads 4`: 3930/3930.
- `tools/regression_spotcheck.sh`: 145/145.
- Decode gate NOT run (no dav1d on this host) — known coverage gap.

========================= 4. REMAINING MAPPED GAPS =========================

- `jnt_convolve_{x,y,2d}` + `convolve_2d_copy_sr` — C registers AVX-512; the
  port has them scalar/v3. Compound/jnt paths are cooler than the `_sr`
  family on these cells.
- `fwd_txfm2d_*_avx512` (lowbd slots) — registered at AVX-512 in C; a deep
  butterfly pipeline, higher effort/risk.
- Wiener lane-utilization gaps (16 vs 32 lanes, i16 madd) — partially open.
